/P 85 0 R
/T (How do you find your own "voice" or expression within the structured grammar of the dance? Bharatanatyam is deeply structured, but within that discipline lies room for personal expression. I find my "voice" by fully immersing myself in the music and its meaning and then going beyond it. When I release the pressure to perform perfectly and instead focus on connecting to the piece, something genuine comes through. That connection allows me to embody characters through my own perspective, and in doing so, hoping to speak to the audience in a way that is authentically mine.)
/E (How do you find your own "voice" or expression within the structured grammar of the dance? Bharatanatyam is deeply structured, but within that discipline lies room for personal expression. I find my "voice" by fully immersing myself in the music and its meaning and then going beyond it. When I release the pressure to perform perfectly and instead focus on connecting to the piece, something genuine comes through. That connection allows me to embody characters through my own perspective, and in doing so, hoping to speak to the audience in a way that is authentically mine.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
