/T (What is the most difficult part of translating a specific theme or poem into movement, and how did you overcome that hurdle during rehearsals? During rehearsals, I constantly questioned whether a gesture or expression accurately conveyed the intended Bhava, since even a slight change in movement could alter the rasa, or the emotional experiences the audience receives. One of the most difficult parts was maintaining a clear emotional intention throughout the entire performance. I am continuing to work on overcoming this hurdle by closely observing and working with my gurus and peers, taking the time to understand their interpretations and energy. )
/E (What is the most difficult part of translating a specific theme or poem into movement, and how did you overcome that hurdle during rehearsals? During rehearsals, I constantly questioned whether a gesture or expression accurately conveyed the intended Bhava, since even a slight change in movement could alter the rasa, or the emotional experiences the audience receives. One of the most difficult parts was maintaining a clear emotional intention throughout the entire performance. I am continuing to work on overcoming this hurdle by closely observing and working with my gurus and peers, taking the time to understand their interpretations and energy. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [14]
>>
