448 0 obj
<<
/Title (Was there a specific varnam passage that felt like a breakthrough moment for you? How did it change your perspective on your training? The chittaswaram in the varnam was my greatest challenge, technically demanding and mentally exhausting to master. But pushing through it, showed me something I now carry into every aspect of my training: focused determination is the difference between a passage that defeats you and one that defines you)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 396 0 R
>>
endobj
449 0 obj
<<
/Title (If you were expecting a green juice or a handful of almonds, I hate to disappoint. For nearly a decade, my pre-performance ritual has been, without fail - a Crunchwrap and nacho fries from Taco Bell. Something about that combination just settles me before I step on stage, and at this point I'm not willing to mess with the formula. Call it comfort, call it superstition - either way, it works.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 397 0 R
/Next 450 0 R
>>
endobj
